course: dictionary
lesson: 10272
title: Topple: falling over and losing power
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Topple has two main meanings, and the words around it show which one you need. «Standing still on a bike you topple at once, but when you ride you hardly have to think.» Here topple means to become unsteady and fall over, because you wobble and tip off the bike.
explain: The second meaning is about power. «In 1911 an uprising in the city of Wuchang toppled the Qing» means the uprising made the rulers lose their power. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence: "made the Qing lose their power" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Topple often links to balance. A tall tower with a narrow base topples easily, while a wide base helps it stand. When something is unsteady and about to fall, topple is the word to think of.
fact: To topple means to become unsteady and fall over, or to push something so that it falls.
fact: To topple a leader or government means to make them lose power.
fact: «Topple over» and «topple down» both mean fall, and «be toppled» means someone was pushed out of power.
fact: A tall tower with a narrow base topples more easily than one with a wide base.
fact: Topple changes its form: topples, toppled and toppling.
exercise: «Standing still on a bike you topple at once.» What does topple mean here? | Ride very fast in a circle | Ring a bell | Shine brightly | *Become unsteady and fall over
exercise: «In 1911 an uprising toppled the Qing.» What does toppled mean in this sentence? | Invited them to a party | Painted them a new colour | *Made them lose power | Built them a tall tower
exercise: Which tower is most likely to topple? | A low tower with a wide, flat base | A short tower with a wide base | A tower built on a wide base that stands firm | *A tall tower with a narrow base
test: «A girl in Texas snatched a toy, and a three-year-old toppled backwards off a step.» What does toppled backwards mean? | *Fell over backwards | Jumped forward onto the step | Walked slowly away | Stood up very straight
test: Which phrase means the same as topple over? | Shout very loudly | Grow taller and stronger | *Fall over | Stay perfectly still
exam: Which sentence uses topple to mean make a ruler lose power? | Ride your bike slowly around the park | Standing still on a bike you topple at once | *In 1911 an uprising in the city of Wuchang toppled the Qing | A tower of blocks toppled in the middle of the room
